<.shell title="Tables" current={:tables}>
  <h1>Tables</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    32px rows by default, 24px when compact. Cells line up on their first line of text, so a
    row with a wrapped cell still reads across.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Text at sm (14px). Headers semibold on <code>--surface-alt</code>, and they stick on scroll.
    </li>
    <li>Numbers right-aligned with tabular figures. Codes, such as letter numbers, in mono.</li>
    <li>
      Sortable headers show an arrow, or ⇅ when the column sorts both ways. The sorted column is
      underlined in primary and has <code>aria-sort</code>.
    </li>
    <li>Actions in a row are small buttons or links.</li>
    <li>
      Columns go in order of use: what identifies the row first, then what people act on, then
      the rest. IDs and contact details go last.
    </li>
    <li>
      On a phone, tables scroll sideways rather than reflow. A short table used on a phone, such
      as the door's, stacks each row instead with <code>.table-stack</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Activities</h2>
  <p>The activity list: filters, a summary line, the table, and pages.</p>
  <div class="example">
    <form class="filter-form" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input id="f-q" name="q" label="Search" value="" />
      <.input
        id="f-kind"
        name="activity"
        type="select"
        label="Kind"
        options={[
          {"All", "all"},
          {"Incident", "incident"},
          {"Exercise", "exercise"},
          {"Event", "event"}
        ]}
        value="all"
      />
      <.input
        id="f-when"
        name="when"
        type="select"
        label="When"
        options={[{"All", "all"}, {"Current", "current"}, {"Past", "past"}, {"2025", "2025"}]}
        value="2025"
      />
      <.input
        id="f-sort"
        name="sort"
        type="select"
        label="Sort"
        options={[{"Date ↓", "date-"}, {"Date ↑", "date"}]}
        value="date-"
      />
    </form>
    <div class="table-summary">
      <span class="table-summary-links">
        <.a href="#">Current</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">Future</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">Past</.a>
        ·
        <.a href="#">All</.a>
      </span>
      <span class="table-summary-count">1,912 activities</span>
    </div>
    <.activity_table
      id="sample-activities"
      rows={activities()}
      sort="date-"
      path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
      team={sample_team()}
    />
    <.pagination class="my-p" paginated={sample_page()} path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end} />
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.activity_filter_table&gt;</code>. Filters are <code>&lt;.input&gt;</code>s in a <code>.filter-form</code>, and the table is <code>&lt;.activity_table&gt;</code>, shown here with made-up activities.
  </p>

  <h2>Tax credit letters</h2>
  <p>A header row over a group of columns, and an action in a row.</p>
  <.table
    id="sample-letters"
    rows={letters()}
    class="table-striped"
    sort="total"
    path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
  >
    <:header_row>
      <th></th>
      <th colspan="3">SARVAC hours</th>
      <th colspan="3"></th>
    </:header_row>
    <:col :let={r} label="Name" class="whitespace-nowrap" sorts={[{"↑", "name"}]}>
      <a href="#" class="link">{r.name}</a>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Primary" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "primary"}]}>{r.primary}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Secondary" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "secondary"}]}>
      {r.secondary}
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Total" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "total"}]}>
      <strong>{r.total}</strong>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Letter" class="w-px">
      <a :if={r.letter} href="#" class="link mono">{r.letter}</a>
      <.button :if={!r.letter} variant={:success} size={:sm}>Create letter</.button>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Email">{r.email}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="ID" class="w-px" align="right" sorts={[{"↑", "id"}]}>{r.id}</:col>
  </.table>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app:
    <code>&lt;.table id="…" rows=&#123;…&#125; sort=&#123;@sort&#125; path_fn=&#123;@path_fn&#125;&gt;</code>
    with a <code>&lt;:col label="…" sorts=&#123;[&#123;"↓", "total"&#125;]&#125;&gt;</code>
    for each column. A column that sorts both ways lists 2 sorts, such as <code>[&#123;"↓", "date-"&#125;, &#123;"↑", "date"&#125;]</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Attendance recommendations</h2>
  <p>Check the changes to make, then perform them.</p>
  <form class="example" onsubmit="return false">
    <.table id="sample-recommendations" rows={recommendations()} class="table-striped table-stack">
      <:col :let={r} label="" class="stack-check">
        <.input :if={r.op != :not_invited} type="checkbox" name={"r-#{r.name}"} checked />
      </:col>
      <:col :let={r} label="" class="stack-full">
        <.badge :if={r.op == :not_invited} kind={:danger}>Not signed up</.badge>
        <span :if={r.op == :add} class="text-success-1 font-bold">Add</span>
        <span :if={r.op == :remove} class="text-danger-1 font-bold">Remove</span>
      </:col>
      <:col :let={r} label="Name" class="stack-title">{r.name}</:col>
      <:col :let={r} label="Email" class="stack-full break-all">{r.email}</:col>
      <:col :let={r} label="Phone">{r.phone}</:col>
    </.table>
    <.form_actions class="mt-4">
      <.button variant={:success}>Perform checked changes</.button>
    </.form_actions>
  </form>
  <p class="spec">
    The markup of the recommended changes in <code>Web.ActivityAttendanceLive</code>. Below 640px each row stacks.
  </p>

  <h2>Wrapping cells</h2>
  <p>Long text wraps; the other cells stay on its first line.</p>
  <.table id="sample-wrapping" rows={rule_preview()} class="table-striped">
    <:col :let={{name, _why, _detail, _days}} label="Member" class="whitespace-nowrap">
      <.a href="#">{name}</.a>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, why, detail, days}} label="Why">
      {why}
      <.badge :if={days} kind={:warning}>{days} days</.badge>
      <span class="block text-secondary-1">{detail}</span>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={_row} label="" class="w-px">
      <.button size={:sm}>Review</.button>
    </:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>Compact</h2>
  <p>
    24px rows, for long lists people scan rather than read.
  </p>
  <.table id="sample-compact" rows={Enum.take(letters(), 3)} class="table-compact table-striped">
    <:col :let={r} label="Name">{r.name}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Total" align="right">{r.total}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Letter" class="w-px whitespace-nowrap">
      <span :if={r.letter} class="mono">{r.letter}</span>
      <.badge :if={!r.letter} kind={:warning}>No letter</.badge>
    </:col>
  </.table>
  <p class="spec not-yet">
    Not used in the app yet: <code>class="table-compact"</code>. Also ready: <code>table-pin-first</code>, which keeps the first column in place while a wide table scrolls on a phone.
  </p>
</.shell>
